Hmm: will the first `+` zoom in the wide map produce a scale-degenerate transfer? Zooming 2 steps in an 11000-px sheet: view ~1/4 of the sheet width. The wide record's extent spans e.g. 360° → 1/4 = 90°. The narrow record's extent spans ~1.1° → mapped region 90/1.1 = 82x the sheet → clamped to whole sheet → setView returns false → 'scale'. Yes.

